#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:4
msgid ":index:`Submitting ISRCs <ISRC; submitting>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:6
msgid ""
"ISRCs are very useful for identifying tracks and recordings, so it is "
"valuable to add them when you are tagging files. Picard can be used to "
"submit ISRCs to the MusicBrainz database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:8
msgid ""
"You can submit ISRCs for tracks that are already in the MusicBrainz "
"database, provided they have ISRCs available in their metadata. If you have "
"a CD with ISRCs, you can enable the \"Read ISRCs from CD\" option in the :"
"doc:`../config/options_cdlookup` to read them from the CD when you do a disc "
"lookup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:10
msgid ""
"To submit ISRCs, select :menuselection:`\"File --> Submit ISRCs\"` or click "
"the \"Submit ISRCs\" button if you have it included in your action toolbar. "
"Picard will check that the ISRCs are valid, that the same ISRC doesn't "
"appear on more than one track on the release, and that the ISRCs are not "
"already present in the database. If all checks pass, the ISRCs will be "
"marked for submission to the MusicBrainz database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:12
msgid ""
"You will be presented with a list of all tracks and their ISRCs, and can "
"select which tracks will be submitted. Any ISRCs that cannot be submitted "
"due to failing the checkswill be indicated as such, and hovering over them "
"will show the reason why they cannot be submitted. You can cancel the "
"submission if changes are required before submitting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:14
msgid "The steps to follow to submit ISRCs are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:16
msgid "Match your files to a release in the right-hand pane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:18
msgid ""
"Select :menuselection:`\"File --> Submit ISRCs\"` or click the \"Submit "
"ISRCs\" button if you have it included in your action toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:20
msgid ""
"Picard will check the ISRCs and present a list of all tracks and their "
"ISRCs. By default, all tracks with new ISRCs that have passed validation "
"will be selected for submission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:22
msgid ""
"Review the list, deselect any tracks you do not want to submit by clearing "
"the checkbox, and click \"Submit\" to submit the ISRCs to the MusicBrainz "
"database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../usage/submit_isrcs.rst:39
msgid ""
"The submission confirmation dialog will show a list of all tracks and their "
"ISRCs for **every** release appearing in the Album pane. The list will show "
"the status of the ISRCs for each track, and you can select which tracks you "
"want to submit. New ISRCs that cannot be submitted because they are invalid "
"or appear on more than one track will not be allowed to be submitted. You "
"can cancel the submission if you want to make changes before submitting."
msgstr ""
